@startuml
actor "User" as User
participant "AI APP\n(OAuth client)" as App
participant "MCP Gateway\n(Resource Server)" as GW
participant "Authorization Server\n(IdP)" as AS

== Discovery ==
App -> GW : Call MCP endpoint (no token)
GW --> App : 401 Unauthorized\nWWW-Authenticate: Bearer\nresource_metadata=".well-known/oauth-protected-resource"
App -> GW : GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource
GW --> App : Protected Resource Metadata (RFC 9728)\nauthorization server + canonical resource URI
App -> AS : GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
AS --> App : AS metadata (RFC 8414)
opt no client credentials yet
  App -> AS : Dynamic Client Registration (RFC 7591)
  AS --> App : client_id
end

== User login ==
App -> User : Open browser to authorization endpoint\n(code flow + PKCE, resource=<gateway URI>)
User -> AS : Authenticate and consent
AS --> App : Redirect with authorization code
App -> AS : Token request (code + code_verifier + resource)
AS --> App : Access token (audience = gateway) + refresh token

== Authorized call ==
App -> GW : Retry call with Authorization: Bearer <token>
note over GW : Validate signature / introspect\nCheck audience = this gateway\nCheck expiry and scopes\nDerive user identity from token subject
GW --> App : Proceed with tool discovery / tool call\n(scoped to this user)

== Renewal ==
App -> AS : Refresh token grant (token expired)
AS --> App : New access token
note over User, AS : User logs in again only when\nthe refresh token expires or is revoked
@enduml
